{
  "note": "Ground truth for the token estimator: a prompt's character-class census beside the provider's own input count for it. Two provenances, and a case says which it is. `recorded` - the census is the one llm_request_fingerprint.census carried for that request, so it is measured data and any call site and any prompt size can produce one. `reconstructed` - the case predates that field, when the log carried lengths only; its census was rebuilt from the material the call had carried and is an approximation, which is what tokenizerTokens exists to bound. Recorded verbatim from agent.jsonl in both: id (requestId), callSite, recordedAt, messages and recordedMessageChars (llm_request_fingerprint.messageCount/messageCharLengths), actualInputTokens (calibration_sample.actual) and recordedEstimateAtTheTime (llm_request_fingerprint.estimatedInputTokens). No prompt text reaches this file.",
  "fittedAgainst": "scripts/derive-recorded-prompts.py writes this file. A `recorded` case is a direct read of the log - census and provider count joined on the request - and needs neither the vault nor a tokenizer; the script keeps the worst estimator error per (callSite, size band), so the cases pin where the rules are weakest rather than where they are comfortable. The nine `reconstructed` cases were derived by the older procedure, which rebuilt each census from this repository's prompts/*.md and templates/*.md sized by the recorded prompt_breakdown subtotals plus the JSON-escaped code and prose of sourceNote, kept a case only when the census summed to recordedMessageChars exactly, the pre-fix 1.9/4.2 rules reproduced recordedEstimateAtTheTime within 3%, and the DeepSeek-V3 tokenizer counted the rebuild within 3% of actualInputTokens. That procedure could reach only ingest.synthesize and only prompts above ~3.4k tokens, because nothing else emits prompt_breakdown - the debt the census field closes. The script preserves them on rebuild: they cannot be re-derived, and the 17.6k case is the only large one there is. The character-class rates themselves were fitted separately against tokenizer counts over 973 real texts; the script's docstring states that procedure.",
